    "presentation": {
      "chief_complaint": "Fever and fatigue",
      "hpi": "The patient is admitted with fever and fatigue, not with a finished explanation. Temperature is 38.60 C. Dental examination shows caries and periodontal disease. There is no prosthetic valve. Two blood-culture sets drawn before antibiotics grow Streptococcus gordonii, reported susceptible to penicillin. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily is started after the cultures are drawn. Repeat cultures show no growth. Transesophageal echocardiography shows a mitral vegetation, mild regurgitation, no abscess, and preserved ventricular function. Cardiac surgery finds no current indication for an operation. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily continues for four weeks from the first negative culture. Lisinopril is continued. Creatinine stays 0.8 to 0.9 mg/dL and discharge blood pressure is about 130 mm Hg systolic. Aspirin is continued for known coronary disease. Metformin is continued. Glucose is 137 mg/dL at discharge and he is eating.",
      "review_of_systems": null,
      "presenting_symptoms": [
        "Nausea"
      ],
      "symptom_duration": "two days",
